<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottone Visconti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1207–<a href="/years/1295">1295</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ottone Visconti was Archbishop of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> from 1262 and the founder of Visconti power in the city. Long kept out of Milan by the ruling della Torre family, he defeated them at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-desio">Battle of Desio</a> in 1277 and took control of the city. He secured the succession for his great-nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matteo-i-visconti">Matteo I Visconti</a>, who became imperial vicar in 1294.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ottone-visconti.jpg" alt="Ottone Visconti" width="320" height="245" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ingresso_di_Ottone_Visconti_a_Milano.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
